Conditional statement: if
Used to conditionally execute a block of code
Syntax

if (expression) {
statement1
statement2
}

if (isPrime) {
System.out.println("prime");
System.out.println("hurray!");
}

If expression is true, statement are executed.
if is a reserved word in Java

