Conditional statement: if else
Used to conditionally execute one of two blocks of code
Syntax

if (expression) {
statement1
if (isPrime) {
statement2
System.out.println("prime");
}
}
else {
else {
statement3
System.out.println(“not prime");
statement4
}
}
If expression is true, the first block is executed. Else, the second block is executed.
else is a reserved word in Java
